{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vedq6wYmZEjX89ce96BmK8","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n\nAI_GUIDE.md:596:**Light guns (Time Crisis, The House of the Dead, Virtua Cop).** Start from the 3D FLIGHT slice's rails (or a 2D screen of `overhead` sprites): the camera rides an `E.Path` (`world.camera` following the rail's point), foes pop out from behind cover on a script by distance, and the player aims with the pointer: a click (a tap on a phone) at `input.pointer()` hits the nearest foe whose `world.project(x, y, z)` point lies within its size on the screen of it and that the camera sees (`world.clear` from the camera's pose); the reticle is drawn at the pointer. Reload by shooting off the screen (or a button); a pedal to take cover (a button that lowers the camera behind cover). Each enemy's shot is telegraphed by a ring that closes.\nAI_GUIDE.md:629:  - A Gallery scene plays every skill and monster for visual review.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174731__x326e4b/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbb0a1ea-12f9-46f9-9677-d2d253a967c8","uuid":"ebc98ff4-95b2-43ea-8e0e-a3e4d6e7644c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:49:52.051Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n\nAI_GUIDE.md:596:**Light guns (Time Crisis, The House of the Dead, Virtua Cop).** Start from the 3D FLIGHT slice's rails (or a 2D screen of `overhead` sprites): the camera rides an `E.Path` (`world.camera` following the rail's point), foes pop out from behind cover on a script by distance, and the player aims with the pointer: a click (a tap on a phone) at `input.pointer()` hits the nearest foe whose `world.project(x, y, z)` point lies within its size on the screen of it and that the camera sees (`world.clear` from the camera's pose); the reticle is drawn at the pointer. Reload by shooting off the screen (or a button); a pedal to take cover (a button that lowers the camera behind cover). Each enemy's shot is telegraphed by a ring that closes.\nAI_GUIDE.md:629:  - A Gallery scene plays every skill and monster for visual review.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174731__x326e4b/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Vedq6wYmZEjX89ce96BmK8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
