{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyduZNdn13b1zCU5RXM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ShFUvdt9nkcPmzyTb81nM6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/x326e4b-research/engine/dist/handoff && grep -n \"shapeParts\\|resolveShape\\|shapeMesh\\|E\\.shapeBox\\|shapeSprite =\\|function resolve\\|materialTile\\|E\\.shapeSprite\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20; grep -n \"shapeParts\\|shapeBox\\|materialTile\\|shapeSprite\\|E.PATTERNS\\|E.tones\\b\" API-INDEX.md | head -12","description":"Look for shape-resolving and material helpers in the engine"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4501,"cache_read_input_tokens":179144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4501},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbb0a1ea-12f9-46f9-9677-d2d253a967c8","uuid":"780d9249-e8c2-4631-bcc6-ffaef35cd6c7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:04.106Z","request_id":"req_011CggyduLyrxJxX33YMUzaW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01ShFUvdt9nkcPmzyTb81nM6":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/x326e4b-research/engine/dist/handoff && grep -n \"shapeParts\\|resolveShape\\|shapeMesh\\|E\\.shapeBox\\|shapeSprite =\\|function resolve\\|materialTile\\|E\\.shapeSprite\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20; grep -n \"shapeParts\\|shapeBox\\|materialTile\\|shapeSprite\\|E.PATTERNS\\|E.tones\\b\" API-INDEX.md | head -12","description":"Look for shape-resolving and material helpers in the engine"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShFUvdt9nkcPmzyTb81nM6","type":"tool_result","content":"1850:   * opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1,\n5681:function resolveMat(q) {\n8171:function resolveShape(S, o = {}, name) {\n8365:  const R = resolveShape(S, Object.assign({}, o.params, { mats: o.mats }), o.name), facing = o.facing === undefined ? Math.PI / 2 : o.facing, k = scaleOf(S, o), a = facing - Math.PI / 2;\n8469:  const R = resolveShape(S, Object.assign({}, o.params)), b = [1e9, 1e9, 1e9, -1e9, -1e9, -1e9], all = [], contact = [];\n8568: * a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view:\n8573:E.shapeSprite = (id, o = {}) => {\n8591: * a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg })\n8601:E.shapeMesh = (id, o = {}) => {\n8603:  const R = resolveShape(S, Object.assign({}, o.params, { mats: o.mats }), typeof id === 'string' ? id : undefined), k = S.scale || 1, groups = new Map(), b = [1e9, 1e9, 1e9, -1e9, -1e9, -1e9];\n8618:/** a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units\n8622:E.materialTile = (id, o = {}) => {\n8631:/** where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip,\n8634:E.shapeBox = (id, x, y, z = 0, o = {}) => {\n8677:  const b = E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z, o); if (!b) return null;\n12395:      let sp = this._shapes.get(key); if (sp === undefined) { if (this._shapes.size > 300) this._shapes.clear(); sp = E.shapeSprite ? E.shapeSprite(id, { view: v, facing: f, size: o.size || 1 }) : null; this._shapes.set(key, sp); }\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n797:- `E.PATTERNS`: the patterns, by name: (s, m) => a tone step (-1 .. +2) at a point s of a surface, for a material m's numbers. Add your own: E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0\n798:- `E.PATTERNS.bark(s)` †: fissures running up a trunk; a cut end shows its rings\n799:- `E.PATTERNS.bricks(s, m)` †: running bond, bw x bh (6 x 3), mortar a step darker (mortar: its step)\n800:- `E.PATTERNS.cloth(s, m)` †: a fine weave and soft folds (fold .9)\n801:- `E.PATTERNS.crate(s, m)` †: a framed and braced crate side (frame 2 wide, a diagonal brace, boards bw 3 inside); lids are planks\n802:- `E.PATTERNS.foliage(s, m)` †: leaf clumps (size 3.5), each lit at its top and dark at its foot, a few bright leaves\n803:- `E.PATTERNS.glaze(s)` †: a glossy shine where the light is strongest, a few specks\n804:- `E.PATTERNS.metal(s, m)` †: hard light (a shine where lit, darker in shade); rivet: a rivet every rivet units\n805:- `E.PATTERNS.noise(s, m)` †: soft patches (scale 4)\n806:- `E.PATTERNS.none()` †: the light's bands alone\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174731__x326e4b/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbb0a1ea-12f9-46f9-9677-d2d253a967c8","uuid":"5b562589-e3f3-46e3-ba3f-a0a0ebc0b8aa","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:04.127Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1850:   *