{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018q7DXeNbhyJKgpZdi5Kwgr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tide Crisis 3\n2\t\n3\t**The title.** As TASK.md asks, I brainstormed 50 riffs on *Time Crisis 3* without showing them, then picked one with an\n4\tOS-entropy RNG (`python3`, `secrets.randbelow(50)` → #9). In file names it is `TideCrisis3`, and the source is\n5\t`TimeCrisis3`.\n6\t\n7\t**The pitch.** Tide Crisis 3 is an original arcade light-gun shooter on rails, drawn in my-3D2dge's PS1-era pixel style\n8\tand played in first person. Two agents of C.R.E.S.T. (Covert Response & Emergency Strike Team) fight to take an island\n9\tcity's tidal barrier back from a disgraced admiral before the dawn king tide drowns the city. You take cover to dodge\n10\tand reload, then pop out to shoot. You switch between four weapons, read the \"crisis flash\" that marks every shot that\n11\tcan hit you, and beat the clock in every area. You can play alone, with two players on one machine (split screen), or\n12\twith 1–4 players online in an AI Hub session.\n13\t\n14\t**The core loop** (write this sentence at the top of the game code): *the camera rides the rail to the next area (WAIT)\n15\t→ ACTION! starts the clock → pop out and shoot → duck when a crisis flash says a shot will hit → reload in cover →\n16\tclear the area before TIME runs out → ride on → beat the boss → STAGE CLEAR.*\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## Contents\n21\t0. Read this first: deliverables, rules, environment, glossary\n22\t1. The game: what we keep from the source, pillars, modes, length\n23\t2. Source information (verified at planning time)\n24\t3. Technology and architecture\n25\t4. Systems (each with its spec, numbers and tests)\n26\t5. Content: world, cast, tone, enemies, stages, bosses, script, art, animation, audio\n27\t6. Build order and milestones\n28\t7. Risks and how to de-risk them\n29\t8. Testing\n30\t9. Done checklist (every TASK.md requirement, and where this plan covers it)\n31\t\n32\t---\n33\t\n34\t## 0. Read this first\n35\t\n36\t### 0.1 Deliverables (exact names, all in this folder)\n37\t| What | Name |\n38\t|---|---|\n39\t| Dev folder (every dev file lives here) | `TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174731/` |\n40\t| The game, one self-contained HTML file | `TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174731.html` |\n41\t| Exit interview (exactly TASK.md's shape; check that it parses) | `exit-interview.json` |\n42\t\n43\tThe HTML inlines the patched engine, the game and the AI Hub session client. It plays from `file://` with no network.\n44\tSource Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback go in three places: the in-game About/Credits\n45\tscreen, `exit-interview.json`, and the final chat reply. Generate all three from one data file (`src/99-about.js`,\n46\t§4.14) so they agree.\n47\t\n48\t### 0.2 Golden rules\n49\t1. **Original world, original cast.** The source gives us a genre and a feel, nothing more (§1.1). Never use its names,\n50\t   levels, music, logos or UI art."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbb0a1ea-12f9-46f9-9677-d2d253a967c8","uuid":"7f592afa-590f-4a3d-8b85-77e6fcf752d8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:29:39.443Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174731__x326e4b/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Tide Crisis 3\n\n**The title.** As TASK.md asks, I brainstormed 50 riffs on *Time Crisis 3* without showing them, then picked one with an\nOS-entropy RNG (`python3`, `secrets.randbelow(50)` → #9). In file names it is `TideCrisis3`, and the source is\n`TimeCrisis3`.\n\n**The pitch.** Tide Crisis 3 is an original arcade light-gun shooter on rails, drawn in my-3D2dge's PS1-era pixel style\nand played in first person. Two agents of C.R.E.S.T. (Covert Response & Emergency Strike Team) fight to take an island\ncity's tidal barrier back from a disgraced admiral before the dawn king tide drowns the city. You take cover to dodge\nand reload, then pop out to shoot. You switch between four weapons, read the \"crisis flash\" that marks every shot that\ncan hit you, and beat the clock in every area. You can play alone, with two players on one machine (split screen), or\nwith 1–4 players online in an AI Hub session.\n\n**The core loop** (write this sentence at the top of the game code): *the camera rides the rail to the next area (WAIT)\n→ ACTION! starts the clock → pop out and shoot → duck when a crisis flash says a shot will hit → reload in cover →\nclear the area before TIME runs out → ride on → beat the boss → STAGE CLEAR.*\n\n---\n\n## Contents\n0. Read this first: deliverables, rules, environment, glossary\n1. The game: what we keep from the source, pillars, modes, length\n2. Source information (verified at planning time)\n3. Technology and architecture\n4. Systems (each with its spec, numbers and tests)\n5. Content: world, cast, tone, enemies, stages, bosses, script, art, animation, audio\n6. Build order and milestones\n7. Risks and how to de-risk them\n8. Testing\n9. Done checklist (every TASK.md requirement, and where this plan covers it)\n\n---\n\n## 0. Read this first\n\n### 0.1 Deliverables (exact names, all in this folder)\n| What | Name |\n|---|---|\n| Dev folder (every dev file lives here) | `TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174731/` |\n| The game, one self-contained HTML file | `TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174731.html` |\n| Exit interview (exactly TASK.md's shape; check that it parses) | `exit-interview.json` |\n\nThe HTML inlines the patched engine, the game and the AI Hub session client. It plays from `file://` with no network.\nSource Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback go in three places: the in-game About/Credits\nscreen, `exit-interview.json`, and the final chat reply. Generate all three from one data file (`src/99-about.js`,\n§4.14) so they agree.\n\n### 0.2 Golden rules\n1. **Original world, original cast.** The source gives us a genre and a feel, nothing more (§1.1). Never use its names,\n   levels, music, logos or UI art.","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1671}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018q7DXeNbhyJKgpZdi5Kwgr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
